            <div xml:id="d785">

                <pb facs="0738" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg734"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/705: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-30T18:00:00-04:00">June 30, 1938—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>418. Your 899, June 24, 5 p.m., in regard to Chinese customs. Please ascertain,
                    if practicable, the list of “items favorable to the <pb facs="0739" n="735"
                        xml:id="pg735"/> Japanese” that must “be implemented in full” before
                    contributions will be made by Japanese-controlled areas toward loan payments,
                    and inform the Department and Tokyo.</p>
                <p>Please repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
